# Propolis Release Notes

## 0.1.2 (19 Nov 2026)

* No changes to the app. The tests now close the stores they open, so they
  pass with warnings treated as errors.

## 0.1.1 (19 Nov 2026)

* Propolis now talks to GitHub, and to Propolis on your other Macs, using
  httpx2, the maintained continuation of httpx.
* Secure connections are checked against the certificates your Mac trusts,
  instead of a list bundled with the app.

## 0.1.0 (19 Nov 2026)

A rebuild of the app. Triage works as it did in 0.0.1: threads stay in their
labels in the order you filed them, labels can flag on activity, and only
activity that needs a response from you counts. What's around it is new.

* Unread and Done views, beside the Inbox and your labels. Threads you clear on
  github.com go to Done the next time Propolis starts, unless they have a
  label.
* A toolbar, with Add by Number, Refresh, Open on GitHub, Mark as Read, Mark as
  Done and Unsubscribe, a Label menu that adds or takes off any label, and a
  Filter menu.
* Mark as Read (⇧⌘U) and Unsubscribe (⇧⌘M). Unsubscribing also marks the
  thread as done.
* Label several threads at once, by selecting them and pressing a label's
  number.
* Search the current view by title or repository. The Filter menu lists the
  types, reasons and repositories in the view, with how many threads each
  would show.
* An address bar above the reading pane, with Back, Forward and Reload. Links
  to other sites open in your browser.
* Icons coloured by state, as on GitHub, and icons for commits, CI runs,
  Dependabot and security alerts, and invitations.
* Labels as coloured pills beside the address of the thread you're reading,
  and a yellow alert icon on threads that need attention.
* Settings (⌘,).
* Threads you add by number are checked for activity every 10 minutes.

Upgrading from 0.0.1: 0.1.0 keeps its data in the same place, but doesn't read
0.0.1's labels, triage history or GitHub sign-in, so it starts with the default
labels and asks you to sign in again. It keeps 0.0.1's list of accounts, and
leaves 0.0.1's labels and history as they are. To share an inbox with another
Mac, use 0.1.0 on both of them.

## 0.0.1 (03 Nov 2026)

* Initial release
